event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"mcp_09d827a3e775df43016abb6b9857e887d28a98109cdbac83ac","type":"mcp_call","status":"completed","approval_request_id":"mcpr_09d827a3e775df43016abb6b96e57487d292f889537d7c35cd","arguments":"{\"repoName\":\"cequence-io/openai-scala-client\",\"question\":\"Which ws-client version does this project depend on? Please identify the dependency version from the build files.\"}","error":null,"name":"ask_wiki_question","output":"The project `cequence-io/openai-scala-client` depends on `ws-client` version `1.0.0` . This version is defined in the `Dependencies.scala` file  and used across various `build.sbt` files for different modules     .\n\n## `ws-client` Version Definition\n\nThe `wsClient` version is centrally defined in `project/Dependencies.scala` :\n```scala\nobject Dependencies {\n\n  object Versions {\n    val wsClient = \"1.0.0\"\n    val scalaMock = \"6.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n\n## Usage in Build Files\n\nThis `wsClient` version is then imported and used in the `libraryDependencies` of several `build.sbt` files for different modules:\n\n*   **`openai-core/build.sbt`**: Uses `wsClient` for `ws-client-core-akka` and `json-repair` .\n    ```scala\n    libraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core-akka\" % wsClient,\n      // we ship our own version of json-repair (originally in Python)\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"json-repair\" % wsClient,\n    ```\n    \n\n*   **`openai-client/build.sbt`**: Uses `wsClient` for `ws-client-core` and `ws-client-play-akka` .\n    ```scala\n    libraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient,\n    ```\n    \n\n*   **`openai-client-stream/build.sbt`**: Uses `wsClient` for `ws-client-core`, `ws-client-play-akka`, and `ws-client-play-akka-stream` .\n    ```scala\n    libraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka-stream\" % wsClient\n    )\n    ```\n    \n\n*   **`anthropic-client/build.sbt`**: Uses `wsClient` for `ws-client-core`, `ws-client-play-akka`, and `ws-client-play-akka-stream` .\n    ```scala\n    libraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka-stream\" % wsClient,\n    ```\n    \n\n*   **`google-vertexai-client/build.sbt`**: Uses `wsClient` for `ws-client-core` and `ws-client-play-akka` .\n    ```scala\n    libraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n      \"com.google.cloud\" % \"google-cloud-vertexai\" % \"1.52.0\",\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient,\n      \"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient\n    )\n    ```\n    \n\n## Notes\n\nThe `ws-client` library is a sibling library managed manually, as indicated in the `.scala-steward.conf` file, which explicitly ignores updates for `io.cequence` group IDs . This suggests that its version is controlled directly within the project rather than through automated dependency updates . The `CHANGELOG.md` also mentions the migration to `io.cequence:ws-client-*:1.0.0` as a significant change .\n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Module Architecture (cequence-io/openai-scala-client)](/wiki/cequence-io/openai-scala-client#1.2)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/which-wsclient-version-does-th_820448b9-66a0-4ff6-84b9-e7682b86bb8f\n","server_label":"deepwiki"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":12}

